%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
title: a1 Situated Activities
syntax: xwiki/2.1
%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
**Abstract.** Situated Activities record what stakeholders do today, under the conditions they actually do it in. Main concept: **Meaningful Connections**. The morning-care concept is a separate strand, listed below.

= In brief =

* A newcomer arrives among strangers, confused and with little say (SA-01).
* Others have stayed in their rooms for months, waiting for a reason to come out (SA-02).
* Shyness, forgotten names and having nothing to say stop most first contacts (SA-03).
* Fewer still talk, held back by fear of a "no" or of intruding (SA-04).
* Staff introduce residents when they have time, and know only some shared pasts.

